      "page_level_design_instruction": "NEONRIFT HOME PAGE \u2014 VISUAL DESIGN PLAN\n\nSIGNATURE MOMENT: The hero section deploys a full-bleed, diagonal-panel split where the headline \"THE GRID DOES NOT FORGIVE THE WEAK.\" is set in Archivo Black at an extreme condensed display scale (clocking ~18\u201322vw character height), rendered in Neonrift Cyan (#00F5FF) with a Rift Magenta (#FF0080) glitch-channel offset duplicate shifted 6\u20138px on the X-axis \u2014 a chromatic aberration / glitch-separation effect. This headline does not sit politely inside a text column; it bleeds horizontally across the full viewport width, overlapping the cyberpunk arena illustration behind it, with the bottom edge of the type crossing into the illustration layer. This is the defining cyberpunk typographic stunt for this page \u2014 inevitable for the aesthetic, impossible to mistake for any other brand.\n\nSECTION SEQUENCE & RHYTHM:\n1. Hero (home-section-1) \u2014 Full-bleed, maximum density, illustration-behind-type, diagonal panel cut at bottom edge. Dark and electric.\n2. Stats (home-section-2) \u2014 A high-contrast horizontal marquee-style stat strip. Sparse vertically, dense horizontally. Acid Circuit numerals dominate. Zero illustration.\n3. Feature Grid (home-section-3) \u2014 2\u00d72 card grid on Grid Steel surface. Moderate density. Scanline texture overlaid. Asymmetric header block offset left.\n4. Timeline (home-section-4) \u2014 Vertical indexed list with large left-side node numbers and a horizontal scanline rule connecting them. Alternates dense/sparse. Trophy icon anchors the final node as a visual exclamation.\n5. CTA (home-section-5) \u2014 Full-bleed Rift Magenta panel. Maximum contrast. Minimal copy. Centered by exception \u2014 the aesthetic and structural logic of a closing CTA block demand it here, creating a deliberate punch after the asymmetric sections above.\n\nCOLOR & SURFACE LOGIC ACROSS SECTIONS:\n- Section 1 (Hero): Void Black (#0A0A0F) base, Plasma Violet (#7B00FF) gradient radiating from center-bottom behind illustration, Neonrift Cyan type, Rift Magenta glitch offset and CTA button.\n- Section 2 (Stats): Grid Steel (#1C1C2E) surface. Acid Circuit (#AAFF00) for the oversized numerals. Datastream White (#E8EEFF) for descriptor text. Neonrift Cyan separator glyphs between stat blocks.\n- Section 3 (Feature Grid): Void Black page background, Grid Steel card surfaces with 1px Neonrift Cyan border glow. Rift Magenta used on card eyebrow-level icon accents. Deadzone Charcoal scanline overlay at 15% opacity across entire section.\n- Section 4 (Timeline): Void Black background. Node numbers in Plasma Violet. Active status badge in Acid Circuit. Upcoming status badges in Deadzone Charcoal. Neonrift Cyan horizontal rule connecting nodes. Datastream White body text.\n- Section 5 (CTA): Full-bleed Rift Magenta (#FF0080) background. Void Black headline text. Acid Circuit secondary CTA button outline. This color inversion \u2014 the brand's most aggressive signal color as a full-bleed surface \u2014 is the closing visual shock.\n\nTYPOGRAPHIC HIERARCHY:\n- Display headlines: Archivo Black, ALL CAPS, tight tracking (\u22120.05em), maximum condensed. Cyan or inverted on dark/colored backgrounds.\n- Section eyebrows: Press Start 2P, 9\u201310px, 0.12em letter-spacing, Acid Circuit color, uppercase.\n- Subheadlines: Archivo Bold, ALL CAPS, 0.8\u20131.2rem, Datastream White.\n- Body / descriptors: IBM Plex Mono Regular, 15px, 1.65 line-height, Datastream White or Deadzone Charcoal for muted metadata.\n- Stat numerals: Archivo Black or Press Start 2P at oversized scale (4\u20136rem), Acid Circuit.\n- Timeline node indices: Archivo Black, 5\u20137rem, Plasma Violet, used as structural left-column anchors.\n\nDENSITY / WHITESPACE LOGIC:\n- Hero: Dense. Type and illustration overlap aggressively. Padding compressed to push content toward edges.\n- Stats: Sparse vertically (single horizontal band), dense horizontally (four stat blocks in a row with tight gutters).\n- Feature Grid: Moderate. Cards have internal padding but gutters are tight (16px). Section has generous top padding to breathe after the stat strip.\n- Timeline: Alternates dense node entries with deliberate vertical breathing room between nodes \u2014 the scanline rule provides visual continuity across the whitespace.\n- CTA: Extremely sparse. Two lines of text, two buttons. Maximum breathing room to let the Rift Magenta surface land.\n\nRESPONSIVE BEHAVIOR:\n- Hero: Headline scales from ~18vw desktop to a stacked two-line treatment on mobile, still full-width. Illustration shifts to a bottom-anchored position behind text on mobile.\n- Stats: 4-column horizontal strip collapses to 2\u00d72 grid on tablet, single column on mobile. Numerals scale down proportionally.\n- Feature Grid: 2\u00d72 on desktop, 1\u00d72 on tablet, 1\u00d71 stacked on mobile. Cards maintain full border-glow treatment at all breakpoints.\n- Timeline: Vertical layout is already mobile-friendly. Node numbers scale from 6rem to 3.5rem on mobile. Horizontal connecting rule becomes a vertical left-border line.\n- CTA: Centered stack remains centered. Buttons stack vertically on mobile.\n\nDESIGN SYSTEM FIT:\nEvery color token, typeface, and visual cue (glitch accents, scanline patterns, diagonal panels, neon signage energy) traces directly to the shared design system and aesthetic guidance. The page introduces no motifs outside those inputs. The diagonal panel cut at the hero bottom edge recurs as a subtle 4\u20136\u00b0 skewed section divider between sections 1\u21922 and 4\u21925, creating a structural rhythm device that is distinctly cyberpunk without being decorative noise.",
